  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current implementation uses SLSQP optimization on upscaled versions of the parent solution, which may be limited by local minima and gradient-based search. We propose a more robust approach using Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO), which is better suited for non-convex optimization problems and can explore multiple regions of the solution space simultaneously. PSO avoids getting trapped in local minima through its population-based search and swarm intelligence mechanisms.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Decision variable: h \u2208 [0,1]^n, where \u222bh dx = 1\n- Objective: min h max_k [h \u22c6 (1 - h)](k)\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = n/2\n- The correlation is computed as (h \u22c6 (1 - h))[k] = \u2211x h[x](1 - h[x+k])\n- Feasibility repair: After each iteration, clip h to [0,1] and normalize to maintain \u2211h = n/2\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na. Initialize:\n   - Use initial_h_values if available; else, create a default with a central pulse\n   - Upsample to 280 points using linear interpolation\n   - Normalize and clip to ensure feasibility\n\nb. PSO setup:\n   - Population size: 50 particles\n   - Inertia weight: 0.9 initially, decreasing to 0.4 over time\n   - Cognitive/social coefficients: 1.5 each\n   - Velocity limits: [-0.5, 0.5]\n\nc. Iterative optimization:\n   For each particle:\n   1. Evaluate objective via cross-correlation\n   2. Update personal best\n   3. Update global best\n   4. Update velocity and position\n   5. Repair feasibility: clip and normalize\n\nd. Termination:\n   - Max iterations: 500\n   - Early exit if no improvement in 75 iterations\n   - Must respect time budget constraints\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Population size: 50 (balance between diversity and compute)\n- Initial velocity: random uniform [-0.1, 0.1]\n- Inertia decay rate: 0.95 per iteration\n- Velocity clamping: \u00b10.5 (prevents excessive jumps)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Estimated runtime: ~200s per particle\n- With 50 particles and 500 iterations: ~5000s\n- Implemented with early exit on time budget\n- Robustness: maintains feasibility through repair step\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Final solution must pass feasibility checks\n- Objective evaluated with exact task metric\n- Intermediate results validated at each PSO step\n- Fallback mechanism: return initial_h_values if needed",
